ScummVM Wii U / Aroma — experimental SDL2 port
=============================================

Version 0.7.0 includes SCUMM v0-v8, MM/Xeen, SCI/SCI32, Mohawk/Myst/Riven,
Blade Runner and Groovie/Groovie2, with MP3, Vorbis and MT-32. It retains the
renderer fix, fixes SDL zero-timeout waits, speeds up Curse/QFG4 IO and Groovie
RGBA conversion, and improves existing-text editing/controller keyboard input.
See RELEASE-0.7.0.md for hardware results and remaining limitations.

Apply these incremental patches to devkitPro/SDL wiiu-sdl2-2.32 in order:
  1. sdl2-swkbd-input.patch
  2. sdl2-swkbd-lifecycle.patch
  3. sdl2-renderer-lifecycle.patch
  4. sdl2-timer-zero-timeout.patch
  5. sdl2-swkbd-controller.patch
  6. sdl2-rgba565-blit.patch
Then rebuild/install SDL and relink ScummVM. Do not apply a patch twice.
The local SDK compatibility adjustments listed below are also retained.

Requires devkitPPC, WUT, the devkitPro Wii U SDL2 port, target zlib and
wut-tools (elf2rpl and wuhbtool). DEVKITPRO must identify the same SDK used
to build SDL2; DEVKITPPC and WUT_ROOT may be set explicitly.

Build outside the source tree, after activating the SDK:
  /path/to/scummvm/configure --host=wiiu --disable-all-engines \
    --enable-engine=scumm --disable-detection-full --disable-mt32emu
  make -j2 wiiu_release

The above is the historical minimal build, not the 0.7.0 release profile.
For all release engines and MP3/Vorbis/MT-32, with diagnostics disabled:
  bash backends/platform/sdl/wiiu/build-release.sh
See EXPERIMENTAL.md for historical JPEG/MP3 dependency preparation. For pinned
libogg 1.3.6/libvorbis 1.3.7 sources, activate the SDK, set WIIU_CODEC_DIR to a
separate source/build directory and run build-vorbis-sdk.sh. The release helper
checks required features and generates Xeen mm.dat version 1.3 using the host
generator (no game files needed). Do not replace it with upstream mm.dat 1.2.

This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.
libjpeg-turbo 3.1.4.1 and libmad 0.15.1b notices are in licenses/ (source tree)
or scummvm/doc/LICENSES/ (installation package). The integrated Munt emulator
uses LGPL-licensed code; its license is also included. Roland ROMs are not.

The existing ScummVM SDL backend supplies software rendering, mixer,
events, timers and mutexes. SDL handles GX2, audio and ProcUI. Static
engines only. No RetroArch, networking or OpenGL is used.

The output filename is ScummVM.wuhb. Both the long and short Wii U Menu
names are ScummVM, without a version suffix. The menu icon reuses the
upstream 128x128 ScummVM asset at dists/psp2/icon0.png; no new artwork or
external image conversion tool is required. wuhbtool embeds the icon.

Copy the CONTENTS of wiiu_release/ onto the SD card. Merge directories:
do not replace an existing scummvm directory or delete existing saves.
  wiiu/apps/ScummVM.wuhb
  scummvm/data/          themes, translations and enabled engine data
  scummvm/doc/           licenses and this document

For community testing without Aroma, make wiiu_release_all also stages
wiiu_rpx_release/ with wiiu/apps/scummvm/ScummVM.rpx, meta.xml, the same data
and documentation, and README-RPX.md. Package the two staging directories
separately. The RPX is the same executable embedded in the WUHB; it has not
been verified through Homebrew Launcher or a non-Aroma environment. Do not
claim legacy compatibility from successful RPX generation alone.

Start ScummVM from the Wii U Menu under Aroma. The backend creates:
  scummvm/scummvm.ini
  scummvm/scummvm.log    overwritten at the next launch; copy before retrying
  scummvm/saves/

Games are not included; browse the SD using Add Game.
WUT paths are /vol/external01/... (not sd:/... in configuration files).
The GamePad is joystick 0. Touch uses ScummVM's existing SDL finger
handling, with direct positioning by default. GameController mappings
and ScummVM keymaps supply buttons and the virtual mouse. Use launcher
Quit or HOME to exit; verify HOME/return before testing long sessions.
Negative joystick indices are overridden because opening the GamePad is
also required for touchscreen events.

Native keyboard:
- Fields requesting ScummVM's virtual keyboard feature open the Wii U
  keyboard on the GamePad. Minus opens it manually via the standard global
  "Display keyboard" / JOY_BACK binding (unless the user remapped it).
- OK inserts the submitted text; it does not press Save/Enter for you.
  Wait for the name to finish appearing before saving. Characters are sent
  at 100 ms intervals for original SCUMM dialogs that keep one key per tick.
- Cancel dismisses only the keyboard, without inserting text or sending Esc.
- Supported ScummVM fields and original SCUMM labels supply existing text for
  editing. Confirm replaces the changed suffix; unchanged/Cancel leaves it
  intact. Other engine fields may still use insertion-only behavior. Original
  dialogs keep their own length/character restrictions.
- Controller selection no longer depends on the output display; missing input
  samples are polled for native keyboard input, including a late GamePad.
  Native keyboard resources are cancelled/released before HOME foreground
  memory release. Pro-only/HOME behavior still needs hardware confirmation.
- Keep ENABLE_VKEYBD disabled: this uses SDL's native keyboard, not the
  separate ScummVM keyboard pack. SDL's Wii U SYSWM submission events and
  multi-chunk UTF-8 text are handled by the small Wii U event adapter.
- This build also requires the accompanying local SDL GamePad fix for
  releases consumed by swkbd and for held OK/Cancel input leaking on close.
  See sdl2-swkbd-input.patch (apply in devkitPro/SDL wiiu-sdl2-2.32).

Default in-game mouse controls: left stick moves, A left-clicks, B
right-clicks, and holding R slows the pointer. GUI actions can differ.

Validation:
- SDK smoke test: I tested it on my Wii U (video, input, touch, audio,
  SD, zlib, timer/thread, HOME/return and clean shutdown).
- Launcher: I tested it on my Wii U and captured screenshots and a clean
  shutdown log. I also tested Sam & Max Hit the Road and Indiana Jones and
  the Last Crusade, including saving, sound and controls.
- Native keyboard: I tested it successfully on my Wii U on September 26, 2026.
- Menu icon: I confirmed it worked on my console on September 28, 2026.
- Standalone RPX through non-Aroma loaders: awaiting community hardware tests.

The local SDK used devkitPPC r50 (GCC 16.1.0/newlib 4.6), WUT v1.9.1,
devkitPro SDL2 2.32.7 (wiiu-sdl2-2.32, a8f1e43a), zlib 1.3.2 and
wut-tools 1.3.4. Besides sdl2-swkbd-input.patch, the local SDK has compatibility
changes: WUT lock_try_acquire_recursive returns int to match newlib; WUT's
Makefile uses -Wno-error=format; SDL's KPADReadEx error variable uses
KPADError instead of int32_t. Account for these when reproducing this SDK.

Keyboard test: create a NEW save with a multi-letter name in both games;
verify the whole name arrives once, save and reload. Test Cancel without
changing a name, reopen using Minus repeatedly, and check A/B, stick and
touch immediately after closing. Also test a launcher text field, HOME
return, and clean exit. Keep the previous working WUHB/ZIP as a fallback.
Copy scummvm/scummvm.log before a second launch (it is overwritten).
